1
00:00:00,130 --> 00:00:01,420
So what we built… it's PILL.

2
00:00:02,070 --> 00:00:04,660
Pill is a hardware and software device

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:06,270
So why are we talking about pills?

4
00:00:06,730 --> 00:00:09,790
Pills go through a very intense
process with the FDA.

5
00:00:10,037 --> 00:00:14,647
They go through this process several
times before a normal pharmacy,

6
00:00:14,647 --> 00:00:15,587
like Walgreens,

7
00:00:15,907 --> 00:00:19,137
I got this from Walgreens: aspirin 81.

8
00:00:19,453 --> 00:00:22,983
In the final process, some of them
could be malfunctioned,

9
00:00:22,983 --> 00:00:27,093
and people could have bad intentions and
put different drugs in here.

10
00:00:27,203 --> 00:00:29,963
First we put in the
prescription of the drug,

11
00:00:30,253 --> 00:00:34,443
and then what it looks like.

12
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:38,730
What we have in this beautifully
3D printed device:

13
00:00:38,730 --> 00:00:43,620
we put some water in there, to a
marking, just like so.

14
00:00:43,907 --> 00:00:47,237
As I click start, I push this medicine in.

15
00:00:47,237 --> 00:00:50,437
Now that it's ready, we go
through the countdown.

16
00:00:50,663 --> 00:00:55,733
We use an Arduino UNO Q for the
main head and CPU.

17
00:00:56,113 --> 00:01:02,633
Red, blue and white lights, and a
photoresistor at the back.

18
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:07,400
We use these three colors to find
a good measurement.

19
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:10,730
As the timer runs out, it's
going to check.

20
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:13,500
And oh no: UNABLE TO VERIFY.

21
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:15,750
Because I put morphine in here
instead of aspirin.

22
00:01:16,650 --> 00:01:17,610
So watch out.

23
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:20,600
Please swallow the right pills.

24
00:01:21,070 --> 00:01:21,790
Thank you.

25
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:25,390
